WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.157
Organizations, as well as
employees, can benefit from

00:00:08.158 --> 00:00:11.492
creating a thoughtfully
designed, accessible workspace.

00:00:12.359 --> 00:00:15.565
It opens up a creative sandbox
where people are free to

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.300
think, work and create in a
way that works best for them.

00:00:20.093 --> 00:00:21.180
Inclusive recruiting.

00:00:22.237 --> 00:00:26.617
For people on the neurodiversity spectrum,
interviews can be a challenge because

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:31.385
their communication styles are not similar
to those of neurotypical candidates.

00:00:32.682 --> 00:00:37.380
The robust communication and eye contact
that recruiters and employers look for is

00:00:37.381 --> 00:00:39.380
not the strong suit of 
candidates on the spectrum.

00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:42.160
Try to diversify your hiring strategy.

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:45.647
Psychometric assessments
are far more objective

00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:49.100
as they eliminate human biases
in early stages of recruitment.

00:00:50.931 --> 00:00:54.260
Provide multiple opportunities to
candidates so that they can demonstrate

00:00:54.261 --> 00:00:59.297
their ability and competency during the
process, regardless of neurodiversity.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.077
Formalize a hiring
program to help create a

00:01:03.102 --> 00:01:05.901
talent pipeline of
neurodivergent candidates.

00:01:06.711 --> 00:01:08.140
Distraction-free environment.

00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:11.495
Provide a distraction-free
workspace to employees.

00:01:11.565 --> 00:01:15.891
For example, noise-canceling headphones to
reduce sensory overload and spacious

00:01:15.916 --> 00:01:18.948
drawers and storage cabinets
to declutter their desks.

00:01:20.651 --> 00:01:23.637
Distraction need not 
necessarily be physical.

00:01:24.372 --> 00:01:26.480
Mental decluttering 
is also as important.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.120
Provide reference materials, worksheets,
and interview questions in advance and

00:01:32.121 --> 00:01:34.500
have sufficient mental health 
days in your company calendar.

00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:38.900
Assistive technologies can help some
neurodivergent employees to perform better.

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:44.740
Such support can include software and
devices like portable and talking word

00:01:44.741 --> 00:01:48.500
processors, assistive listening
systems, and visual organizers.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.356
Architectural accommodations.

00:01:52.247 --> 00:01:57.296
You can create focused areas of work where
employees, neurodiverse or neurotypical,

00:01:57.523 --> 00:01:59.655
can choose to work 
with low stimuli.

00:02:00.928 --> 00:02:05.392
Assess the texture of desks, chairs,
and any other high-touch surfaces.

00:02:06.564 --> 00:02:10.540
Spatial disorientation can frustrate
people with dyslexia and autism.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:17.276
So try to create unique spaces with visual
landmarks and clear lines of sight that

00:02:17.301 --> 00:02:20.338
can help everyone map their
own location within a space,

00:02:20.771 --> 00:02:23.021
ultimately saving both
time and frustration.

00:02:24.517 --> 00:02:26.420
Arranging furniture
in different ways can

00:02:26.421 --> 00:02:28.700
also help people feel
better equipped at work.

00:02:29.314 --> 00:02:32.620
The same positioning of the desk might
not be comfortable for everyone.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.420
So allow a space where pacing is welcomed.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:38.996
Flexibility.

00:02:40.035 --> 00:02:42.987
Consider giving your employees 
the option of remote working.

00:02:44.151 --> 00:02:47.600
Flexible work schedules support 
your entire workforce and not just

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:52.370
neurodivergent employees, working parents,
caregivers, and people with disability.

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:54.792
Empowering language.

00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:59.512
Neurodiversity advocates encourage
inclusive, non-judgmental language.

00:03:00.277 --> 00:03:03.980
While many disability advocacy
organizations prefer person-first

00:03:03.981 --> 00:03:06.664
language, a person with autism,

00:03:06.688 --> 00:03:09.380
a person with Down
syndrome, some research

00:03:09.381 --> 00:03:11.804
has found that the majority
of the autistic community

00:03:11.976 --> 00:03:15.900
prefers identity-first
language and autistic person.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.188
Therefore, rather than making assumptions,
it's best to ask directly what a person's

00:03:22.407 --> 00:03:25.720
preferred language is and how 
they want to be addressed.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.200
Educate your team.

00:03:29.154 --> 00:03:31.822
Create a culture where
individuals feel comfortable to

00:03:31.847 --> 00:03:34.678
disclose and talk openly
about their neurodiversity.

00:03:35.787 --> 00:03:39.345
Upscale your workforce by providing
diversity and inclusion training days

00:03:39.517 --> 00:03:42.022
for all so that everyone
understands the challenges

00:03:42.046 --> 00:03:44.681
and the uniqueness
of neurodiversity.

00:03:46.307 --> 00:03:49.980
Focus on fostering an open and trusting
relationship with your team.

00:03:50.773 --> 00:03:52.983
Ask the employees what
 support they need.

00:03:53.795 --> 00:03:56.659
Provide employees additional
support and guidance if required.

00:03:57.073 --> 00:04:00.452
And ensure to make employees aware 
of the availability of the same.

00:04:01.546 --> 00:04:03.204
Ensure other team
members are aware of the

00:04:03.229 --> 00:04:06.054
specific needs each
individual may require.

00:04:06.414 --> 00:04:10.140
Moreover, handle performance
issues very sensitively.

00:04:10.294 --> 00:04:13.890
If you feel uncertain about anything,
you can begin by asking your employees

00:04:14.085 --> 00:04:17.738
what they feel is required for them to
work efficiently and comfortably.

00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:21.130
Your employees do not
have to reveal their medical

00:04:21.155 --> 00:04:23.382
history for you to make
accommodations at the workplace.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.306
You can simply ask them to share which 
elements of their work experience

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.407
could be made more 
inclusive or accessible.